## 203-to-V2 mapping taxonomy

Every V1 record must have a row in an eventual machine-readable crosswalk with:

`legacy_id,legacy_status,legacy_evidence_sha,current_evidence_sha,decision,successor_ids,owner_domain,notes`

`decision` allowed enum:

- `PRESERVED_DONE`: the original evidence is still valid and no new implementation requested.
- `VERIFY_AGAIN`: old evidence was SHA/fixture-limited or nonproduction.
- `PARTIALLY_IMPLEMENTED`: code exists, acceptance not demonstrated.
- `SPLIT`: epic-sized old item decomposes into unique bounded work packets.
- `MERGED`: several old entries overlap a single canonical new task (all source IDs preserved in crosswalk).
- `SUPERSEDED`: later code/ADR invalidates proposed earlier implementation and replacement documented.
- `DEFERRED`: intentionally outside release slice, not deleted.

Acceptance: 203 input IDs, 203 unique mapped entries, zero orphan task, zero active duplicate owner, zero erroneous DONE from checkbox-only inference.

## Ownership boundaries (no accidental new app)

- **Dock** public released or explicitly demo-tagged experience; data owner is never Dock itself.
- **Headquarters** authenticated content stewardship, governance, research and SHADOW/100CENTER workspaces.
- **Cockpit** local process/runtime operator controls. Never a second HQ governance interface.
- **ARSY** existing single Fastify MoonQL backend currently named `apps/radio`; migration via accepted ADR M28 only.
- **AI Gateway** model/provider transport with opt-in policy; never research truth authority.
- **Sentinel** source collection with egress control, never publisher or final reviewer.
- **MoonUI** shared components/tokens; **Moonframe** separate candidate contracts, not forced into production.

Canonical entity owners remain D00–D13 per BLUEPRINT (Corpus, UNILEX, Ontology, Actors, Research, Witness, Story, Governance, Signal, World, Journey, Workflow, Design).

